{"title":"Career Roadmap — Quantitative Analyst","role":"Quantitative Analyst","summary":"A Quantitative Analyst (Quant) uses mathematics, statistics, programming, and data analysis to solve complex problems involving financial markets, risk, pricing, trading, portfolio optimization, and investment decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Mathematics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Quantitative Analyst (Quant) uses mathematics, statistics, programming, and data analysis to solve complex problems involving financial markets, risk, pricing, trading, portfolio optimization, and investment decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Sc Mathematics student, this is a strong but highly competitive career. Mathematics provides an excellent foundation, but students should deliberately add:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Probability","Statistics","Financial Mathematics","Python/C++","Data Structures & Algorithms","Finance"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"There are several quant career directions:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quantitative Research"},{"text":"Quantitative Trading"},{"text":"Risk Analytics"},{"text":"Derivatives Pricing"},{"text":"Portfolio Analytics"},{"text":"Algorithmic Trading"},{"text":"Financial Data Science"},{"text":"Model Validation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For the most technically demanding quant-research and trading roles, an M.Sc/M.Tech/MFE or other quantitative PG degree is strongly recommended, although exceptional bachelor's graduates can enter directly."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Development Focus","Typical Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Mathematics, probability, statistics, Python, algorithms"},{"text":"Mathematics Student / Quant Intern"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Quant finance + advanced statistics + pro